  "id": "DrugBank_DB00635 - MONDO_4980",
  "verbalization": "Prednisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Atopic Eczema through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve corticosteroids. The evidence suggests that Prednisone, through its indication for Fetal Erythroblastosis and subsequent relationships with Hydrocortisone Acetate and Methylprednisolone, ultimately leads to the condition Atopic Eczema. These corticosteroids are known to modulate immune responses, reduce inflammation, and affect skin physiology, which are key mechanisms in the development of atopic eczema. The shared pathway through different corticosteroid analogs highlights a potential mechanism of action that is broadly applicable across these compounds. While the exact mechanism linking Prednisone to Atopic Eczema remains to be fully elucidated, the cumulative evidence points to a role of corticosteroids in the pathophysiology of the condition.",
